<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2"><Document><name>ILLUSTRATIVE electron-strix14-2026-11-27 ascent (3DOF sim)</name><description>FLOWN 2026-11-27. T0 is the actual liftoff 2026-11-27T00:15:00Z (+900 s from the pre-flight window open 2026-11-27T00:00:00Z). LL2 id 2093e4fc-ac8c-4296-a1b5-deececee6a72 is Launch Successful, net 2026-11-27T00:15:00Z, minute precision, last_updated 2026-11-27T04:48:55Z. Rocket Lab mission page: 1:15 p.m. NZDT, 101st launch overall. Rocket Lab mission-success post (dateline 27 November 2026): the StriX satellite was delivered to a 569 km orbit; 22nd launch of 2026 and 101st mission overall. That post writes 27 September 2026 once; September was not used. UTC columns and KML &lt;when&gt; tags shifted +900 s. Elapsed times and ECEF geometry unchanged. Sim not re-run. ILLUSTRATIVE.
ILLUSTRATIVE ASCENT ECEF — Electron &#x27;Night Owls Never Sleep&#x27; (StriX Launch 14) — NOT OFFICIAL TELEMETRY
Method: first-principles 3DOF sim (/workspace/trajectory-deck/sim/ascent3dof.py): WGS-84 rotating Earth, J2, US76 drag,
thrust SL/vac interpolated on ambient pressure, mdot from Isp, staging/fairing/coast events; vertical rise to 8.0 s (rule: config guidance),
pitch kick 3.453 deg over 10 s, gravity turn, linear-tangent upper-stage steering tan(theta)=0.9457-0.002954*(t-t_ign), solved by optimizer.
Vehicle config: Rocket Lab Electron (sim/vehicles/electron.json; every number carries a source URL, derivation, or ASSUMPTION).
Electron: GLOW, S2 propellant, thrusts, Isp, fairing mass/time from Rocket Lab Electron Payload User Guide (7.0 content, 8.0 URL).
DERIVED: S1 propellant (0.90 fraction ASSUMPTION), effective mdot from published burn times; ASSUMED S2 dry 250 kg, Cd 0.4, 8 s vertical rise.
UNTUNED: Rocket Lab has published no mission timeline for Night Owls Never Sleep. Electron Payload User Guide 8.0 generic event times are the hard times (S1 cutoff L+155 s, S2 ignition L+162 s, fairing L+184 s, S2 cutoff L+535 s).
T0 is the mission-page window open 2026-11-27T00:00:00Z (1:00 p.m. NZDT). SOURCE CONFLICT: launch-safety page prints NET 00:05 UTC and 13:00 NZDT, which are not the same instant; LL2 NET is 00:05Z with window 00:00-00:05Z. Those were not used as T0.
Inclination 38 deg is published by Rocket Lab. Azimuth 81.97 deg is the mean bearing to NAVAREA XIV 338/26 debris areas A and B. Non-rotating inclination from that azimuth is 39.94 deg. 38 deg is below the pad latitude, so it is not a reachable non-rotating heading. Azimuth was not retuned.
Single StriX SAR satellite for Synspective. Payload 190 kg is the ASSUMED stack (100 kg class + Kick Stage), not a fit.
File ends 2 revs after S2 cutoff on the inferred insertion orbit. Rocket Lab publishes no deploy time and no Kick Stage burn time for this mission. Kick Stage circularization is not modelled.
Target (see launch config): insertion 230 km, apoapsis 569 km, fpa 0, launch azimuth 81.97 deg; payload 190 kg.
Pad: -39.260881N 177.865826E. Frame: WGS-84 ECEF, positions km, velocities km/s (Earth-relative).
T0 used: 2026-11-27T00:15:00Z. Re-run with another T0 by shifting utc_iso only; ECEF geometry is Earth-fixed.
POST-CUTOFF: deploy time unpublished (Rocket Lab&#x27;s Night Owls Never Sleep mission page and launch-safety page publish no deploy time and no Kick Stage burn time (orbit, inclination, window and hazard areas only, checked 2026-11-24); propagated 2 revs on the inferred insertion orbit). From insertion T+527.0 s the stage is propagated for TWO revolutions (osculating period 93.20 min) on the inferred insertion orbit (same WGS-84/J2/US76-drag model); rows tagged -coast/-burn.
POST-CUTOFF end T+11710 s: inferred insertion orbit, +2 revs (deploy time unpublished): alt 229.87 km, osculating 223.5 x 638.7 km, i 39.846 deg.</description>
